{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian","id":1385346,"title":"PCs: Seeing the face of an Antediluvian","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-05-02T20:00:01-07:00","id":1385346,"title":"PCs: Seeing the face of an Antediluvian","content":"Have any of your characters either in memory or in person seen their Antediluvian forebear? If so, what was their reaction?<br /> <br /> I was running a game earlier this week and my players were going through the memories of The Dracian/Zapathasura/Ravnos himself and in it each player saw the face of their forebear and each had a different reaction:<br /> <br /> The Lasombra was overcome with a great feeling of disquiet.<br /> The Malkavian had a transcendental experience.<br /> Our Gangrel looked upon the face of Ennoia and has found what he wants to hunt most.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T21:42:56-07:00","id":1385349,"title":"","content":"This is a great idea.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-02T21:50:07-07:00","id":1385350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1385349#post1385349\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is a great idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T18:46:06-07:00","id":1385501,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah, there are definitely a ton of different ways that one could go about it, particularly if you go to an almost eldritch level of how horrifying or cataclysmically revelatory seeing such an ancient incarnation of the curse could be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-03T19:32:18-07:00","id":1385515,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gryffon15</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1385501#post1385501\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh yeah, there are definitely a ton of different ways that one could go about it, particularly if you go to an almost eldritch level of how horrifying or cataclysmically revelatory seeing such an ancient incarnation of the curse could be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aside from the obvious Absimiliard, the only &quot;inhuman&quot; looking ones would likely be Tzimisce and Ennoia (you can't go 5k+ years without frenzying for beast marks). Zapathazura would only look like a monster if necessary by Chimerstry.<br /> <br /> Other than his third eye, Saulot looked human. Cappadocious appeared as a wizened old man. Even Lasombra's depictions of his &quot;diablerie&quot; shows him as an old man.<br /> <br /> Seeing even a memory of Malkav would likely ruin someone's day. Who knows how potent his dementation abilities might be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-04T01:00:06-07:00","id":1385557,"title":"","content":"Hmm, now I wonder, if I should have one or more of my players have a run-in with their Ante - without knowing who it is. Pretty sure they can all hide their true identity from their progeny.<br /> <br /> Why? Shits and giggles, maybe. The ancients need some fun too<br /> <br /> But probably I won't do that. Maybe when they get more powerful and might actually be useful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2337-quatar","name":"Quatar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"269"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T04:19:25-07:00","id":1388294,"title":"","content":"In my game where there not 13 but 16 antes there had been two run ins with antes. One whas the Stone Man which came from 2nd Gen that not rebelled onte their creater and the other one whas Salyrion the Ante of Maeghar/Kiasyd. The first one whas more of a coincidence because the Caitiff in my group decides to help the thin blood enklave that hides from the Camerilla and he ran ack wanting to stop there scourges only to find out the Stone Man already erridicated all of them already. Later the encounter of Salyrion whas the typical, you can not bear to be in presence of another one because it remind you what you lost so the tremere in the group tried to find out how mighty this other one is only to loud yelling out, that it is a Antediluvian because he whas so surprised by it. There Salyrion decided now that the cat is out of the bag to tell them the trueth about that he and the stoneman where just embraced to get a second chance in (un)live and the Stone Man is the reason everyone warns about the thin blood bringing the doom. The reason is the Stone Man in our round sees the Thin Bloods as Caitiff too and because they treat them like they have no worth in live (and out of fear of Gehenna) the elder vampire accidentaly bring Gehenna over them like a self fullfilling prophecy with angering the Stone Man and the only one that are safe from his wrath are caitiff, blood lines, the Maeghar/Kiasyd, the clan of vampireninjas which stays in Nippon and those that have reached Golconda.<br /> <br /> The result is in a newfound intemidating respect for the Caitiff the Tremere decided to go after Salvetion and reach Golconda with the first action releasing his housegargoyle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T12:17:11-07:00","id":1388384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian#post1385346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have any of your characters either in memory or in person seen their Antediluvian forebear? If so, what was their reaction?<br /> <br /> I was running a game earlier this week and my players were going through the memories of The Dracian/Zapathasura/Ravnos himself and in it each player saw the face of their forebear and each had a different reaction:<br /> <br /> The Lasombra was overcome with a great feeling of disquiet.<br /> The Malkavian had a transcendental experience.<br /> Our Gangrel looked upon the face of Ennoia and has found what he wants to hunt most.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes they did. They killed a couple in my chronicle of Ages (and no, it was not them rolling dices, it was the culmination of a chronicle of ages ending in Gehenna and they did what was required to weaken the antediluvians enough to get a fighting chance).<br /> <br /> But before that they had met Cappadocius (the chronicle start was in 1197 so he was still active) and Lasombra. Both were unpleasant experiences for the PCs. Both accepted to meet the PCs who needed information from them and both got something in exchange. Cappy presented himself as small bald monk but none of the players were able to move a muscle in his presence until he had (gently) made his point and then allowed them to ask their questions. Lasombra presented himself as a living liquid shadow taking many forms and none, he gave them a list of things he wanted done before he sent them the information they asked for. I used the experience to foreshadow Cappadocius' madness (his apparent love for God and the will to subsume the creator unto himself) and hint that Lasombra had ways to split his soul among several of his progeny (they also discovered Lasombra had many more childer than the few &quot;official&quot; ones).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T12:55:54-07:00","id":1388400,"title":"","content":"I did run a game where the entire coterie was mass embraced in one night, the sire explained the usual stuff and then left the childer to survive on their own merits. The players managed to do alright until the local Prince requested his Tremere advisor check the PCs bloodwork at which time everyone learned the entire coterie was actually consisting newly made 4th generations.<br /> <br /> I had kept this twist secret from the players so that more experienced among them could enjoy the surprise and be faced with the dread coming from the fallout. On one hand everyone wanted to diablerize them on sight, but on the other hand their existence meant there was an active antediluvian wandering about and probably keeping an eye on the coterie.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T13:39:09-07:00","id":1388416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1388400#post1388400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did run a game where the entire coterie was mass embraced in one night, the sire explained the usual stuff and then left the childer to survive on their own merits. The players managed to do alright until the local Prince requested his Tremere advisor check the PCs bloodwork at which time everyone learned the entire coterie was actually consisting newly made 4th generations.<br /> <br /> I had kept this twist secret from the players so that more experienced among them could enjoy the surprise and be faced with the dread coming from the fallout. On one hand everyone wanted to diablerize them on sight, but on the other hand their existence meant there was an active antediluvian wandering about and probably keeping an eye on the coterie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nice. Very nice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T14:05:54-07:00","id":1388426,"title":"","content":"If you want a sample of what an encounter with an Antediluvian could be like play the Witcher 3, specifically the expansion. There's a plotline leading you to meet with someone who by all means and purposes is an antediluvian for the world of the Witcher. Try to antagonize or wear his patience thin and see how it goes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T14:56:22-07:00","id":1388442,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thoth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1388400#post1388400\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did run a game where the entire coterie was mass embraced in one night, the sire explained the usual stuff and then left the childer to survive on their own merits. The players managed to do alright until the local Prince requested his Tremere advisor check the PCs bloodwork at which time everyone learned the entire coterie was actually consisting newly made 4th generations.<br /> <br /> I had kept this twist secret from the players so that more experienced among them could enjoy the surprise and be faced with the dread coming from the fallout. On one hand everyone wanted to diablerize them on sight, but on the other hand their existence meant there was an active antediluvian wandering about and probably keeping an eye on the coterie.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which clan they where?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-14T21:01:34-07:00","id":1388550,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Koronus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1388442#post1388442\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Which clan they where?</div> </div> </div> </div>I went with Gangrel from a lack of originality and because Ennoia is a relatively easy going Antediluvian, at least compared the some of the other founders. Also it didn't arouse suspicions from the experienced players that a random gangrel embraced some people and left.<br /> <br /> Of course once everyone understood the ramifications of the reveal, I &quot;unlocked&quot; the hidden nine bonus discipline dots I had given everyone at character generation for a total of twelve. I can't say the game was long lasting, but it was fun...\u2026 in a shark tank inside a giant blender kind of way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/727-thoth","name":"Thoth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar727_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1689"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-19T22:38:45-07:00","id":1403623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Quatar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1385557#post1385557\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, now I wonder, if I should have one or more of my players have a run-in with their Ante - without knowing who it is. Pretty sure they can all hide their true identity from their progeny.<br /> <br /> Why? Shits and giggles, maybe. The ancients need some fun too<br /> <br /> But probably I won't do that. Maybe when they get more powerful and might actually be useful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's supposedly an Antediluvian of unclear clan called Lucian. Just like a 8th gen methuselah in Gary that claims to be Gangrel but quite unlike them in many ways. Coincidence? Or hiding in plain sight?\ud83d\ude09","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T08:13:22-07:00","id":1403667,"title":"","content":"I've not read any of the books where these fellows show up, but I feel like Antes, like certain anime characters, would appear to be perfectly normal people until they let that &quot;menacing&quot; aura out.<br /> <br /> <br /> IIRC there was some Demon/Hunter fiction where a hunter finds Lucifer himself, who all the demons had been looking for, and he'd just been walking around like a normal guy. Methinks ancients have their own masquerade to keep up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-20-2020, 11:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T09:34:07-07:00","id":1403678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1403667#post1403667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've not read any of the books where these fellows show up, but I feel like Antes, like certain anime characters, would appear to be perfectly normal people until they let that &quot;menacing&quot; aura out.<br /> <br /> <br /> IIRC there was some Demon/Hunter fiction where a hunter finds Lucifer himself, who all the demons had been looking for, and he'd just been walking around like a normal guy. Methinks ancients have their own masquerade to keep up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So much this. In my games a number of older vampires know a rite that does the inverse of Thaumaturgy 3, just for the convenience of seeming less threatening or tempting to other kindred.<br /> <br /> But then i'm the guy with a game where some clans lost their Antediluvians, others never had them in the first place, a few unknowingly share Founders and some Antes exist that formed no clans, among other little lore twists.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T10:09:20-07:00","id":1403683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1403678#post1403678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But then i'm the guy with a game where some clans lost their Antediluvians, others never had them in the first place, a few unknowingly share Founders and some Antes exist that formed no clans, among other little lore twists.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's... not abnormal. And with the core clans minus the Tremere I wouldn't be shocked if it was revealed that multiple antideluvians had childer so similar they were lumped together in the same clan. But I've never been in a game that ran so close to antideluvians that we'd be aware of that stuff. Best I've seen is a 5th gen, and the first time I saw one of those it was because the storyteller didn't know how big of a deal that was (He was a saddistic sherrif who loved his job but was far too racist for his age) <br /> <br /> So, a little houserule with big, yet setting harmonious, implications; Obfuscate 1 is like an at-will version of the old Arcane background: Basically, the more obfuscate dots you have, the less important you are, the less memorable you are, and when the level's high enough, the more people want to attribute things you did to others, the more people misplace documents concerning you... If your obfuscate exceedes someone's willpower, the effect is even more profound, and for antideluvians with 10 obfuscate.... <br /> <br /> Also Obfuscate 1's hide thing remains as a feature (I also weaken obfuscate 2 so it remains relevant) but the main thing is that obfuscate grants you &quot;arcane&quot;. <br /> <br /> People wouldn't remember the actual antideluvians, they'd just remember stories. <br /> <br /> (all that said, I continue to write on this forum under the assumption that nobody knows my houserules and my -masquerade is solid- arguments do not factor in my houserules; unlike some people I can seperate my way of running things from the books as written)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T14:17:53-07:00","id":1403713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1403683#post1403683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, a little houserule with big, yet setting harmonious, implications; Obfuscate 1 is like an at-will version of the old Arcane background: Basically, the more obfuscate dots you have, the less important you are, the less memorable you are, and when the level's high enough, the more people want to attribute things you did to others, the more people misplace documents concerning you... If your obfuscate exceedes someone's willpower, the effect is even more profound, and for antideluvians with 10 obfuscate....</div> </div> </div> </div>A good houserule, honestly. I don't like disciplines where the lower levels become obsolete when you get higher ones.<br /> <br /> With your permission, I might write this up as a power for V5, because I can think of several characters who would prefer it over the existing level-one Obfuscate powers (V20 &quot;invisible as long as you stand still&quot; and DAV20 &quot;sphere of magical silence&quot;).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T15:00:28-07:00","id":1403717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1403667#post1403667\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've not read any of the books where these fellows show up, but I feel like Antes, like certain anime characters, would appear to be perfectly normal people until they let that &amp;quot;menacing&amp;quot; aura out.<br /> <br /> <br /> IIRC there was some Demon/Hunter fiction where a hunter finds Lucifer himself, who all the demons had been looking for, and he'd just been walking around like a normal guy. Methinks ancients have their own masquerade to keep up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Because of clan curses Ennoia and Absimiliard wouldn't look like normal humans. Absimiliard may appear human with obfuscate but he's supposedly extremely hideous. Ennoia is said to appear as an amalgamation of different bestial features. Tzimisce may appear human but... vicissitude. The rest are very likely to appear human, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23908-kael03","name":"Kael03","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"230"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T15:28:33-07:00","id":1403722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1403713#post1403713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A good houserule, honestly. I don't like disciplines where the lower levels become obsolete when you get higher ones.<br /> <br /> With your permission, I might write this up as a power for V5, because I can think of several characters who would prefer it over the existing level-one Obfuscate powers (V20 &quot;invisible as long as you stand still&quot; and DAV20 &quot;sphere of magical silence&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div>Your description of V20's level 1 Obfuscate just gave me a simple and evil idea for a pretty basic devotion (discipline combo).<br /> Auspex 1, Obfuscate 1 &quot;The Weeping Angel&quot; - the vampire knows instinctively when people are looking or not, when it can move freely unseen and when to stand still to remain invisible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T16:07:41-07:00","id":1403724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Draconis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1403713#post1403713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A good houserule, honestly. I don't like disciplines where the lower levels become obsolete when you get higher ones.<br /> <br /> With your permission, I might write this up as a power for V5, because I can think of several characters who would prefer it over the existing level-one Obfuscate powers (V20 &quot;invisible as long as you stand still&quot; and DAV20 &quot;sphere of magical silence&quot;).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Do as you like; A credit would be cool if you got something published though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-20T19:09:30-07:00","id":1403740,"title":"","content":"The Gangrel antediluvian likely rivals the Eldest Fiend for the title of Most Accomplished Shapeshifter on Earth, so I wouldn't bet the farm on her/it being unable to appear completely unremarkable if she/it wants to.<br /> <br /> The closest any of my characters have come to personally meeting an antediluvian was Shaitan/Huitzilopochtli, which was more than close enough, thank you very much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T07:44:47-07:00","id":1403809,"title":"","content":"The four-generation coterie idea sounds fun, even if utterly insane. I wonder if it would be even more bonkers-fun if it turns out their bloodline can't be traced back to any known clan..?<br /> <br /> As for the Antediluvians' faces. They might look fairly normal, if corpse-like (low humanity and all). Or completely inhuman if my headcanon is right and they're all, or nearly all, trying to transcend their current state.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-21T08:23:20-07:00","id":1403818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1403809#post1403809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The four-generation coterie idea sounds fun, even if utterly insane. I wonder if it would be even more bonkers-fun if it turns out their bloodline can't be traced back to any known clan..?<br /> <br /> As for the Antediluvians' faces. They might look fairly normal, if corpse-like (low humanity and all). Or completely inhuman if my headcanon is right and they're all, or nearly all, trying to transcend their current state.</div> </div> </div> </div>I decided to try out something similar but instead with Kiasyd. Originally I thought of Caitiff but this would make immedeataly let the Cammerila believe the Stoneman rumors or that the clans are a curse instead of a blessing which would way impact to much the so I thought it would be more fun to upgrade a bloodline to a clan of an unknown founder. There whas only the effect, that Marconius Kiasyd turned into Kiasyd Antitribu while the Maeghar where found out and in cooperation with the Tremere there have been experiments where some unmissable victims where brought which where killed and drained and whas about to be embraced by the 4th Gen Kiasyd to find out what exactly whas up with this new clan. Those new embraced that turned out Caitiff from the Maeghar where soon either gifted for diablery or as a payment for the tremere while the newly embraced 5th and 6th gen Kiasyd began to suddenly disappear so some elder can use them for diablery. In the end they where adopted by Shiron, a 4th gen Toreador and set as the prince of munich and after they reached Ancilla status they needed to disparse because their Kiasyd blood did not allowed it for them to continue any longer after they got the right to sire one child. The story ended there so feel free to use it as you see fit.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T13:49:55-07:00","id":1404084,"title":"","content":"I'm not a terrible fan of the Kiasyd, to be honest. Two unique disciplines is a bit much. I'm guessing they lose Obtenebration in your scenario? Since there's no longer a direct link to the Lasombra?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26275,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","user":"Konigheim Horror","date":". 07-22-2020, 07:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T14:13:43-07:00","id":1404088,"title":"","content":"Correct. It whas here because of Toreador Adoption Auspex and Presence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>As I am from Austria I need to clarify two things.<br /> First my native language is german and so please point out if the english I write is broken so I can improve.<br /> Second I do not own VTMV beyond first three books nor any line after M20 Corebook because it is not out there and I wait for the translation.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26160-koronus","name":"Koronus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"366"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-22T14:59:38-07:00","id":1404099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Konigheim Horror</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1404084#post1404084\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not a terrible fan of the Kiasyd, to be honest. Two unique disciplines is a bit much. I'm guessing their lose Obtenebration in your scenario? Since there's no longer a direct link to the Lasombra?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Also they learn Necromancy a lot, typically out of clan .But I guess necromancy is the same thing as obtenebration if you playthe weird edition<br /> <br /> My problem with Kiasyd is that they're such weirdos that i can't imagine them functioning. Like, they're fun, but they're the least believable vampires within the context of the setting. Two rare clan specific disciplines (and necromancy) is a bad thing, since your really shouldn't be using either of those powers for your nightly feeding, and there's only so much you can do with dominate. Kiasyd are like... that highly specialised species that has evolved around a particular plant in a world where that plant isn't that common and is somewhat endangered and.... Generalists are king... Am i being sidetracked here? Mytherceria is cool but it's very much an Auxilery power, so a Kiasyd either exclusively relies dominates for his food (Oh how this can go wrong) or goes tentacle monster on stuff for blood....<br /> <br /> Of course you can just get blood with mundane skills just fine but disciplines should work around improving what you're good at. The Weakness is significant too and you kinda need to... It's too late to go into those details.<br /> <br /> Kiasyd need a slightly more grounded unliving strategy, in my opinion. Three commons is great, two commons and a rare is great, one common and two highly specialised rares is...<br /> <br /> My first thought was to give them obfuscate but I don't know what it should replace. My second thought was making Mytherceria a branch of auspex (Like how Valaren/Quietus have multiple branches) brought about exclusively from fae blood; If you have access to Fae blood, you can buy weird auspex powers. But this is kept a secret because otherwise everyone'd be trying to put a changling in their basement or they'd embrace maeghars to diablerise or... yeah, things'd get bad. At the very least there aren't enough changelings to go around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T11:26:04-07:00","id":1404267,"title":"","content":"Maeghar and Kiasyd, like a lot coming out of the True Hand, set off what would normally be considered red flags if fans wrote it. They're fae-vampires, and they look a bit like elves (unlike actual fae who can look really effin' weird), and they're so special they have TWO or even THREE unique disciplines, and..!<br /> <br /> Obfuscate and Presence both sound quite fitting. Sneaking, hiding, that underscores their overall creepy factor while Presence could be a manifestation of the wonder the fae can evoke in people. So, if the Kiasyd/Maeghar are a clan, I'd say Obfuscate/Dominate/Mytherceria or Obfuscate/Presence/Mytherceria. Which puts them close to the branch family of the Malkavians and the Setites, respectively, which I find makes a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> Tying it back to the original topic: There was some fluff in the revised Malkavian clanbook about how they and the Setites, unlike the other clans, catch a glimpse of their Founders in the last moments before their rebirth into undeath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-23T12:35:03-07:00","id":1404279,"title":"","content":"I don't have a problem with Maeghar. Most players want more than just &quot;it died&quot; as the answer to &quot;what happens if I embrace...&quot; and Maeghar are a good answer. <br /> <br /> But they seem to be perfect serial killers and nothing else. I mean they're weird, they've got an obsession with collecting things, they spent their mortal days living out a weird fantasy that they've been robbed of, and Mytherceria is an exotic discipline for exotic serial killers. They're an interesting antagonist but as player characters it looks like they'll attract the kinds of players who really shouldn't. <br /> <br /> (also I think certain characters would hunt Maeghar down for their powers even if they weren't serial killers)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T07:39:11-07:00","id":1404588,"title":"","content":"Do you have an issue with the Kiasyd then? Just asking for curiosity's sake.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26275-konigheim-horror","name":"Konigheim Horror","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26275_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"95"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-25T16:03:45-07:00","id":1404661,"title":"","content":"Kiasyd are basically flamboyant boss characters. They're like Dracula from Castlevenia: They stay at a castle-like home, They look spectacular even when they don't have guests, they've got all sorts of weird technology and magic and monsters keeping them company, and they don't really belong in the ecosystem of Vampire the Masquerade.<br /> <br /> They're a cool thing but it's painfully obvious someone really wanted to make them a cool thing. The Kiasyd exist either for that snowflake character or for when the storyteller wants to do a daring heist story concerning rarebooks, blood and artifacts but doesn't want to use a chantry and prefers a singular shadow monster and his zombie horde over a bunch of grayfaces, their ghouls and hires, and maybe a gargoyle.<br /> <br /> The Kiasyd sire tutalage phase lasting so long is the only real justification for letting them have two rare disciplines.<br /> <br /> I don't hate them, I just think they're trying too hard. Maybe it's mytherceria. The More I think about it, the more making Mytherceria an Auspex mutation, giving Kiasyd two normal disciplines, would help them fit into the ecosystem a little better... Just look at their discipline spread: How do these guys realistically hunt each night as neonates? If they had a normal appearance, maybe it could be justified.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-25-2020, 07:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T09:21:03-07:00","id":1404788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1404661#post1404661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe it's mytherceria. The More I think about it, the more making Mytherceria an Auspex mutation, giving Kiasyd two normal disciplines, would help them fit into the ecosystem a little better... Just look at their discipline spread: How do these guys realistically hunt each night as neonates? If they had a normal appearance, maybe it could be justified.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mytherceria is the first example I always point to for how V20 has too many distinct disciplines that really should be merged. It's just Auspex with a touch of Dementation and some fae flavor.<br /> <br /> Back in first edition, Malkavians were thematically connected to the fae; perhaps bringing that connection back would help. Since Malks are much more usable in your average VtM game than Weirdlings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","user":"Draconis","date":". 07-26-2020, 12:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T10:50:53-07:00","id":1404802,"title":"","content":"Thematically but not actually. Malkavians are actually connected to everything if you look at them the &quot;right&quot; way. Ravnos have more ties with the fae (because murdering possessed children is the basis of any healthy relationship).<br /> <br /> But Mytherceria is certainly the most extreme example of -needs a merger- (IE I actually agree with it) Even if Serpentis was just protean with a god complex, there were plenty of valid reasons to keep it separate. The non-protean based mergers of a certain edition were purely mergers for the sake of some people like yourself who didn't like how many disciplines there are, but I'd rather have 30 simple disciplines than 10 overstuffed ones. Especially since out of those many simple disciplines I'm only using a few and can put the rest out of mind, whilst with the 10-stuffed model I'm using all of them but only using select powers for each character and.... There's more to memorize. And a lot of the justifications used for the mergers are incredibly flimsy and tend to ignore key details.... and here I am again, off topic and complaining about a crazy idea that somehow became canonical.<br /> <br /> <br /> V20 LotB's Quietus, and how Valeren used to work, are good examples of mergers. Mytherceria is a good example of something needing a merger. Oblivion is an example of why mergers should never happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-26T17:12:11-07:00","id":1404845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1385346-pcs-seeing-the-face-of-an-antediluvian?p=1404802#post1404802\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 LotB's Quietus, and how Valeren used to work, are good examples of mergers. Mytherceria is a good example of something needing a merger. Oblivion is an example of why mergers should never happen.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with you on most of this. (I.e. I think Mytherceria badly needs a merger and Oblivion doesn't work merged.) I just support several of V5's other mergers as well.<br /> <br /> In particular, Serpentis being entirely The Discipline Of Snakes doesn't mesh with the lore of the Setites, who didn't go all-in on the snake thematics until Christianity became popular. If disciplines were actually set in stone by Caine or whatever, how would a discipline's powerset completely change in a mere 2000 years to match a particular cult's branding? The only powers from Serpentis that don't thematically fit Protean are the famous snake eyes and the heart removal, the latter of which has nothing to do with snakes anyway (and should be a ritual instead of a discipline).<br /> <br /> Likewise, the merging of several different sorcerous traditions into &quot;the mechanics are the same, just different paradigms to make them happen&quot; happened back in V20 (if not earlier? I don't remember if Revised ever touched on this). I don't agree with all of V5's decisions on this front, but I do think several V20-era disciplines didn't really fit the five-fixed-powers model, and would work better if liberated from that restriction (e.g. Vicissitude is great thematically but feels badly forced into the five-fixed-powers model).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T00:12:05-07:00","id":1404885,"title":"","content":"Simple things first: <br /> <br /> Blood sorcery (Bar Necromancy and Koldunism) was kinda always the same thing with a different paradigm. In earlier editions however, some traditions had attribute+ability rolls for path powers rather than a willpower roll, and it was also noted that, say, you could learn Thaumaturgy and Assamite sorcery as two different disciplines. It did, however, also say that you could -convert- a foreign paradigm's magic to your chosen path with time and effort (and since that saved xp, of course i'd do that!) In V20's blood magic companion, Rites of the blood, the booked pushed for all path magic to use the same system (Spend blood, roll willpower) and also threw in a bunch of new paradigms to highlight the 'It's all the same stuff just with different paradigms' a bit more. Great book; but it was always a matter of paradigm (except the aforementioned Koldunism and necromancy, the latter of which has a kinda-universal paradigm anyways, which is explained in Rites of the Blood) <br /> <br /> I feel Vicissitude would work with the five power model if the last two were capitalized on. I've always felt terrifying &quot;Schlacta&quot; ghouls were missing the mark in that you can't really make them stronger, so being able to use the princibles of 'zulo' form (Sending the body into overdrive, canibalizing many needed organs for muscle mass and bone growth...) in a limited fashion on ghouls would really tie that power in with the first three as a medical procedure rather than 'I give up, let's copy protean'. The blood form also has particulalry interesting possibilities if you think about what it could mean to turn yourself into a different state and then return to normal perfectly in a powerset of medical marvels: maybe you could move beyond manual sculpting and reform according to will? (A certain problem with this: Bloodform is easily the best of the -becoming immaterial- powers of Protean and obtenebration) <br /> Also Life-to-life should be less than a level 6 power... Perhaps a sorcery combination? <br /> <br /> <b>Serpentis</b>: <br /> I'd sum up Serpentis as <i>Protean through the lense of faith</i> and, if that faith changes, the discipline will evolve. Though I felt DAV20 was far too liberal when it came to how you could customise discipline powers, I've always felt the mandatory snake imagery was far, far too specific for a faith altered power, especially as the different faiths under the setite umbrella had different imagery to capture (There was a at least, a few serpent of the light variations). I always thought the Tlacique really did have a discipline just as much serpentis as it was protean, but the theme was far too different (Skin of the adder became skin of the jaguar) for the settites to really accept it. <br /> <br /> Also the setites took the snake themes from Apep/Apophis in egypt, Set's former foes that might have allied with him against Ra. I don't think they took the snake theme at christianity so much as doubled down on it. (also; Hypothetical before apep 'old clan setite: Obfuscate, Presence, Potence?) <br /> <br /> Heart removal should of course be a ritual rather than a power, which DAV20 did, but also DAV20 took a powerful serpentis and made it more broke so... <br /> <br /> I think the thing is to take away isn't that Serpentis is bad so it's powers should just be thrown in with protean, but rather than serpentis should just get a good writeup (Quietus, amrite?) and intellegently juxtapose itself against protean in a way that affirms Setite and Gangrel beliefs about -the other power- whist doing the same for players looking at these powers from an outside perspective: Just bundling them into the -Choose-at-every-level- paradigm of v5 is a great way to destroy any potential interesting cultural baggage those disciplines might have (But I'm biased because I also know that system is really, really bad in general)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T00:39:18-07:00","id":1404887,"title":"","content":"The Ideal:<br /> <br /> Animalism<br /> Auspex (Mytherceria)<br /> Celerity<br /> Chimestry<br /> Dominate<br /> Dementation<br /> Fortitude<br /> <s>Koldunic sorcery</s><br /> Melepomine (maybe lump this in with Dementation?)<br /> Obfuscate<br /> Obtenebration (abomwe?)<br /> Potence<br /> Presence<br /> Protean (Serpentis, Thanatosis, Visceraticka)<br /> Quietus (sorcerer quietus, Vizier Quietus)<br /> Sorcery, Koldunism (Ogham)<br /> Sorcery, Necromancy<br /> Sorcery<br /> Sanguinis (yep, too different from Vicissitude)<br /> Valeren (Obeah) (Crazy thoughts: Diamonion, Spiritus)<br /> Vicissitude<br /> <br /> 20-23 from 29-32 discipines<br /> Shoving all these into what I think would maybe be 12 disciplines (there are currently 11) would be a disaster. (and, bringing back to the original topic of the thead: would undermine many antideluvians with &quot;unique&quot; disciplines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 07-28-2020, 02:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T16:21:06-07:00","id":1404985,"title":"","content":"Nitpick: you've counted Koldunism twice, and missed a few of the obscure ones like Bardo that nobody cares about.<br /> <br /> If I had the chance to overhaul the system, I'd also personally separate sorcery out from disciplines entirely. The Tremere learn Thaumaturgy and the Giovanni learn Necromancy, not because it's in their blood, but because they have structures in place to teach it (and to keep it secret from outsiders). That cuts the number down a bit more.<br /> <br /> The end result, of course, is that certain clans have unique disciplines and others don't. (Which has always been the case pre-V5.) A few more mergers could help with that, such as giving the Maeghar access to Chimerstry instead of Mytherceria, merging Melpominee with Dementation, maybe finding some way to combine Visceratika with Sanguinis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24808-draconis","name":"Draconis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24808_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-27T23:35:11-07:00","id":1405024,"title":"","content":"Bardo should just be a set of rituals. Have I missed any other obscure ones that lasted more than an edition (I remember there were a few &quot;infernal&quot; disciplines before they got put into DT, Maybe some Gaki disciplines) <br /> <br /> Some disciplines like sanguinis are just so out of the way that there's no real point combining them. (also, you don't want people thinking Blood brothers are normal vampires do you?)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-07-29T19:12:17-07:00","id":1405230,"title":"","content":"I'd be fine with recasting Sanguinus powers as permanent or long-lasting effects of Blood Sorcery rituals by the Blood Brothers' particular creators in the way that Visceratika powers were for Gargoyles in the Dark Ages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}